---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ui, type Lang } from '../../i18n/ui';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const t = ui[lang];
const zh = lang === 'zh';
---

<BaseLayout lang={lang} title={t.navAbout}>
  <section class="section">
    <h1 class="section-title">{zh ? '关于 · 方法论' : 'About & Method'}</h1>

    {
      zh ? (
        <>
          <p>
            本站是一部按时间线与作者双维度组织的中国科幻 / 想象文学图文谱系，
            覆盖从上古神话到当代科幻的完整脉络，并关联影视作品成果。
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">三个内容层级</h2>
          <p>
            为了不混淆历史，站内把收录内容分为三层，并在每张卡片上以徽标显式标注：
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>神话源流</strong>：上古至魏晋的神怪、奇器与异域想象。</li>
            <li><strong>前科幻</strong>：唐宋至清中期的机械、飞行、异域社会想象，尚未建立现代科学框架。</li>
            <li><strong>科幻</strong>：晚清至今，现代科学框架下的想象文学。</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            上古作品不是科幻，而是科学想象的<em>源流</em>。这是本站的学术底线。
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">关于"中国科幻起点"</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>1903 年，鲁迅在《月界旅行·辨言》中引入"科学小说"概念。</li>
            <li>1904 年，荒江钓叟《月球殖民地小说》被公认为中国第一部原创科幻长篇。</li>
            <li>晚清之前没有 genre 意义上的科幻，只有科学想象的萌芽。</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="subhead">收录标准</h2>
          <p>一部作品入库需至少满足两项：中国作者或中文首发；具备科学 / 技术 / 未来社会想象成分；
            有可查证的出版记录；在文学史、口碑或影视作品上具备影响力。每条数据均标注资料出处。</p>

          <h2 class="subhead">图片政策：诚实优先</h2>
          <p>
            全站所有图片均明确标注四级来源之一，徽标显示在每张图右下角。
            目前 84 部作品中实际分布如下：
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>公有领域（16 部）</strong>：古籍书影、清末民初石印本扫描、明清版画等已进入公有领域的图像。
              每张都附带 <code>coverSource</code> 字段记录书名、版本与扫描来源，便于复核。</li>
            <li><strong>AI 生成示意图（68 部）</strong>：当代作品封面——这一层几乎没有公版资源可用。
              全部为「示意图」而非真实封面重制，每张图保留生成 prompt（<code>coverPrompt</code> 字段）以便他人复现或替换。</li>
            <li><strong>已授权：暂无</strong>。本站未与任何出版社、作者、图库签订授权协议。
              若未来获得正式授权，将在原图位显式标注并附授权来源。</li>
            <li><strong>占位图：仅用于影视海报（35 部）与作者头像（31 位）</strong>，
              见下方专项说明。</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="subhead">作者头像：印章而非照片</h2>
          <p>
            作者照片的版权属于摄影者，<em>不属于作者本人</em>。
            本站 31 位作者中既有已故历史人物，也有健在当代作家，
            后者的照片在大多数司法管辖区下受肖像权与摄影著作权双重保护。
            <strong>本站不托管任何作者照片</strong>——
            所有人名位以朱砂印章形式渲染：白文篆体姓名 + 哈希生成的星图纹点缀，
            既保持视觉一致性，又彻底回避肖像权与摄影版权风险。
          </p>
          <p>
            印章里的字统一使用篆体（在 <code>/fonts/seal-zhuan-subset.woff2</code>，
            MIT 协议「余繁新语」子集化部署），中英文页面都用中文姓名，
            因此英文页面不出现拉丁字母首字母缩写。
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">影视海报：版权与替代方案</h2>
          <p>
            电影/电视/动画海报的版权属于制片方或发行方，<strong>不进入公有领域</strong>，
            也不适用合理使用——海报不是文字资料，不属于新闻报道或学术引用的范围。
            因此本站<strong>不抓取、不转存、不热链豆瓣 / IMDb / TMDB 等任何第三方平台的图片</strong>。
          </p>
          <p>
            当前的替代方案（35 部影视作品均采用）：
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>海报位为<strong>类型色 + 类型缩写</strong>的占位图，角标注明「海报待补」。</li>
            <li>每张卡片附<strong>豆瓣 / IMDb 外链按钮</strong>，链接到对方公开搜索页——
              外链本身不构成侵权，读者可自行到原站查看真实海报与评分。</li>
            <li>已有正式豆瓣评分快照的，在卡片正文以文字形式列出（<code>doubanRating</code> + <code>doubanRatingAt</code> 字段注明抓取日期）。</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            未来若获得制片方或版权方的正式授权，将按真实海报替换占位，
            并在下方追加来源与授权号。读者若发现可用的公有领域 / CC 授权海报，欢迎通过 Issue 推荐。
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">多语言与翻译</h2>
          <p>
            本站提供中英双语界面，默认依据访问者系统语言选择（仅当用户未在本站手动切换过时生效）。
            英文条目尚未完成时，页面会显示中文原文并明确标注，<strong>不使用机器翻译填充</strong>——
            机翻的「假英文」对中外读者都是误导，宁可缺。
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">数据纠错</h2>
          <p>
            存疑字段在页面上以问号标注。若发现错漏，欢迎通过仓库 Issue 指正——
            一个数据可信度存疑的资料站是没有价值的，宁可少收，不可错收。
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>
            This archive is a chronological and author-indexed illustrated record of
            Chinese science fiction and the literature of imagination, spanning
            antiquity to the present and linked to film and television works.
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">Three tiers</h2>
          <p>
            To keep the record honest, every entry is assigned one of three tiers,
            shown as a badge on each card:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Myth</strong>: supernatural beings, marvellous machines and distant lands, from antiquity to the Wei–Jin period.</li>
            <li><strong>Proto-SF</strong>: machinery, flight and utopian societies from the Song to the mid-Qing, without a modern scientific framework.</li>
            <li><strong>Science fiction</strong>: from the Late Qing onward, imagination within a modern scientific framework.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Works of antiquity are not science fiction; they are its <em>sources</em>.
            That distinction is this archive's scholarly baseline.
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">On the origin of Chinese SF</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>In 1903 Lu Xun introduced the concept of “science fiction” in his preface to the translation of De la Terre à la Lune.</li>
            <li>Moon Colony Novel (1904) is recognised as the first original Chinese science fiction novel.</li>
            <li>Before the Late Qing there was no science fiction as a genre — only seeds of scientific imagination.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="subhead">Inclusion criteria</h2>
          <p>
            A work is included when it meets at least two of the following: a Chinese
            author or first publication in Chinese; scientific, technological or
            futuristic content; a verifiable publication record; and recognised
            significance. Every entry cites its sources.
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">Image policy: honesty first</h2>
          <p>
            Every image on the site is labelled with one of four provenance levels,
            shown as a badge on the card. The current distribution across 84 works:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Public domain (16)</strong>: facsimiles of classical editions, late-Qing / early-Republic lithographs, Ming–Qing woodblock prints. Each carries a <code>coverSource</code> field naming the book, edition and scanning source for verification.</li>
            <li><strong>AI-generated illustrations (68)</strong>: contemporary book covers, where no public-domain imagery exists. Every AI image is recorded as a <em>schematic illustration</em>, not a reproduction of the real cover; the prompt is preserved (<code>coverPrompt</code> field) so it can be re-rendered or replaced.</li>
            <li><strong>Licensed: none</strong>. The archive holds no licensing agreements with any publisher, author or image library. If formal licenses are obtained in the future, the real cover will replace the placeholder with a clear credit.</li>
            <li><strong>Placeholder</strong>: only used for film / TV posters (35 entries) and author portraits (31 entries) — see the dedicated sections below.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="subhead">Author portraits: seals, not photos</h2>
          <p>
            Copyright in a photograph belongs to the photographer, not the subject.
            The 31 authors range from long-deceased historical figures to living
            contemporary writers, and a living person's portrait is, in most
            jurisdictions, protected by both copyright and personality rights.
            <strong>No author photos are hosted on this site</strong>.
            Every name slot is rendered as a vermilion seal — a vertical Chinese
            name in seal script, with a small starfield derived from a hash of the
            name. Visually consistent, and zero legal exposure.
          </p>
          <p>
            The seal font is <code>/fonts/seal-zhuan-subset.woff2</code>,
            a 38 KB subset of the MIT-licensed typeface <em>Yu Fan Xin Yu</em>.
            Chinese and English pages both use the Chinese name, so no Latin
            initials appear on the English side.
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">Film &amp; TV posters: copyright and the workaround</h2>
          <p>
            A film or TV poster is copyright of the producer or distributor.
            <strong>Posters do not enter the public domain</strong>, and
            fair use / fair dealing generally does not cover them: a poster
            is not the kind of text-based material that news reporting or
            academic citation exists to protect. The site therefore
            <strong>does not scrape, mirror, or hot-link any image from
            Douban, IMDb, TMDB, or any other third-party platform</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Current substitute (used for all 35 entries):
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>The poster slot is a <strong>type-coloured placeholder with a type abbreviation</strong>, with a “Poster pending” tag in the corner.</li>
            <li>Each card carries <strong>Douban and IMDb external links</strong> pointing at the public search page of the other site — a hyperlink is not infringement, and lets the reader see the real poster where they already have an account.</li>
            <li>Where a Douban rating has been snapshotted, it is shown as plain text (<code>doubanRating</code> + <code>doubanRatingAt</code> with the capture date).</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If a formal license is later obtained from the rights holder, the
            placeholder will be replaced and a credit line appended.
            Public-domain or CC-licensed posters are welcome via the issue
            tracker.
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">Languages and translation</h2>
          <p>
            The site is bilingual. The language follows the visitor's system
            setting (unless the visitor has already made a manual choice on
            this site). Where an English entry is not yet written, the
            Chinese original is shown with a clear notice —
            <strong>never a machine translation</strong>. Fake English is a
            disservice to both English and Chinese readers; better to be absent.
          </p>

          <h2 class="subhead">Corrections</h2>
          <p>
            Uncertain fields are marked on the page. Corrections are welcome via the
            repository's issue tracker. A reference site whose data cannot be trusted
            has no value: better to list less than to list wrong.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
